TC-03 manual evidence — Short-lived QR attendance and history
Date: 2026-09-17

Member: phase2.registration.20260916@fithub.test
Staff account: phase2.manual-admin@fithub.test
Credential: freshly generated short-lived QR token; raw token deliberately omitted.

Original run:
- Member generated a QR credential.
- Administrator entered it at /attendance/scanner and selected “Validate and check in QR”.
- Observed result: no request and no attendance row; the form submit handler did not run.
- Decision at this point: FAIL (DEF-001).

Retest after the focused submit-handler fix:
- Generated a new short-lived token.
- Administrator submitted it through the same browser workflow.
- UI message: “Check-in accepted at 9/17/2026, 7:36:25 AM.”
- Reuse of the same credential was rejected with “Check-in token has already been used.”
- Member attendance page showed 1 visit this week, 1 this month, 1 in the membership period, and EUR 29.90 cost per visit.
- PostgreSQL attendance time: 2026-09-17T05:36:25.102869Z.

Final decision: PASS after retest.
Defects: DEF-001 fixed. A follow-up cosmetic field-state issue (DEF-003) was corrected and production-built; a second browser retest of that visual-only correction remains pending.
